                <head>No. 433<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>At the 210th meeting of the National Security Council on August 12, during a
                    discussion of United States policy in the Far East, there was a brief discussion
                    of Thailand, as a result of which the National Security Council, in NSC Action
                    No. 1204–c, “Noted that the President requested the Secretary of State to
                    recommend means of providing visible evidence in Thailand of our intention to
                    prevent further Communist expansion.” (Eisenhower Library, Eisenhower papers,
                    Whitman file) That portion of the memorandum of discussion is printed in <ref
                        target="frus:frus1952-54v12p1/pg_724">Part 1, page 724</ref>.</p>
            </div>
